---------------------------------------------------------

The single-file C release, release/c/wuffs-v0.4.c, from
https://github.com/google/wuffs.

  Copyright 2017 The Wuffs Authors.
  Copyright 2023 The Wuffs Authors.

Distributed under the terms of both the MIT license and the Apache License,
Version 2.0 (the "License"): zupix redistributes it under both and complies
with both. The texts are src/vendor/wuffs/LICENSE, LICENSE-MIT and
LICENSE-APACHE (installed as licenses/wuffs-LICENSE*). Upstream ships no
NOTICE file.

Modified by two patches, and wuffs-v0.4.c carries a notice saying so, as
section 4(b) of the Apache License requires:

  0001-drop-diagnostic-pragmas.patch  removes every "#pragma GCC
      diagnostic" and "#pragma clang diagnostic" line, which R CMD check
      reports;
  0002-drop-unused-swizzle.patch  deletes the one function nothing calls,
      wuffs_private_impl__swizzle_swap_rgbx_bgrx_64, which without those
      pragmas is a -Wunused-function warning.

No other change.

