README.ijg (installed as licenses/libjpeg-turbo-README.ijg), with
libjpeg-turbo's own summary in LICENSE.md (licenses/libjpeg-turbo-LICENSE.md).
This software is based in part on the work of the Independent JPEG Group.

As the IJG License requires, the changes to the original files are these:

  0001-no-stdio-or-exit.patch  changes jerror.c only. error_exit() calls
      zupix's zpx_int_jpeg_error_exit() (src/zpx_jpeg_error.c), which
      returns control to the zupix encoder that called libjpeg, instead of
      calling exit(); output_message() discards the message instead of
      printing it to stderr. An R package may do neither. jerror.c's header
      comment records the change.

No other file is changed. jconfig.h, jconfigint.h and jversion.h, which
libjpeg-turbo's CMake build generates, are not vendored; zupix's own
versions are in src/jpeg-config/.

src/vendor/libwebp/ (libwebp 1.6.0, commit 4fa21912)
---------------------------------------------------

The encoder half of libwebp, from
https://chromium.googlesource.com/webm/libwebp: src/enc, src/utils, the
encoder's part of src/dsp with its SIMD variants, sharpyuv, and the
src/dec and src/webp headers they include. No decoder, mux or demux
library, example or build system is included.

  Copyright (c) 2010, Google Inc. All rights reserved.

Under the BSD 3-Clause License, src/vendor/libwebp/COPYING (installed as
licenses/libwebp-COPYING), with Google's additional patent grant in
src/vendor/libwebp/PATENTS (licenses/libwebp-PATENTS). The authors are
listed in src/vendor/libwebp/AUTHORS (licenses/libwebp-AUTHORS).

Modified by one patch, a backport of a later upstream change:

  0001-backport-rescaler-sse2-casts.patch  applies upstream commit
      220e3d311aad7da6060c3a7380e04a0cdd113a30 (2026-08-06) to
      src/dsp/rescaler_sse2.c: explicit (int) casts on _mm_set_epi32()
      arguments, which silence GCC 16's -Woverflow warning. No change in
      behaviour.

